7 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1045 "30-60-90 Triangles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186060470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059937 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8089f422-4708-55f1-8234-e77b87f79d18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060470 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060470 #edb/ref 1061 10425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060470 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f3aaec85-3c9b-585d-9138-8646ce0db776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060470 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060471 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060471 #edb/ref 1061 10427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060471 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a6377883-059a-5ebf-97b1-38ef2ad683fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060471 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060472 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060472 #edb/ref 1061 10429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060472 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "860a330d-51b9-5aba-a7ce-25da9f5b8254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060472 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060474 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060474 #edb/ref 1061 10432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060474 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ec4f5b67-5c3e-5ce2-bb3a-7b6b95c2a0c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060474 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060475 #edb/ref 1061 10434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060475 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ab1f256a-5f6e-5d12-9b0f-482675761ab1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060475 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060874 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider an equilateral triangle with sides of length $2x$. Notice that any altitude will split it into two congruent triangles, as shown below.\n\n![](images/30/301fe26a314d91d0d316758a5076cea2383f325991789addceaec71f0e7b16dd.png)\n\nIn the new smaller triangle the acute angles will be $30^\\circ$ and $60^\\circ.$ Such triangles are called **$\\boldsymbol{30^\\circ}$-$\\boldsymbol{60^\\circ}$-$\\boldsymbol{90^\\circ}$ triangles**.\n\nBased on the picture above, we see a special property shared by all $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangles:\n\n*In any ${30^\\circ}$-${60^\\circ}$-${90^\\circ}$ triangle, the hypotenuse is twice as long as the shortest leg (which is opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle).*\n\nThis also works in the other direction:\n\n*If the hypotenuse is twice as long as the shortest leg, then the given right triangle is a ${30^\\circ}$-${60^\\circ}$-${90^\\circ}$ triangle.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060874 #edb/ref 1065 2383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060874 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e07c8310-fe8a-5f3e-9ff0-7cd4e93a784c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060874 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060875 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the same ${30^\\circ}$-${60^\\circ}$-${90^\\circ}$ triangle from before. This time, however, we will focus on the height ($h$) instead of the hypotenuse.\n\n![](images/30/301fe26a314d91d0d316758a5076cea2383f325991789addceaec71f0e7b16dd.png)\n\nApplying the Pythagorean Theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2x)^{2} & ={x}^{2}+{h}^{2} \\\\ {h}^{2} & =4{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} \\\\ {h}^{2} & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ h & =\\sqrt{3}x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the second important property:\n\n*In any ${30^\\circ}$-${60^\\circ}$-${90^\\circ}$ triangle, the length of the longer leg (which is opposite the $60^\\circ$ angle) is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the length of the shorter leg (which is opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle).*\n\nWe can summarize everything we know about ${30^\\circ}$-${60^\\circ}$-${90^\\circ}$ triangles using the diagram below:\n\n![](images/85/8598f9163b29833bb5895416e3dec9b6aa2358bd2cfcca944625ebb9f576b3a4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060875 #edb/ref 1065 2386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060875 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e2dbb6c4-dedc-56fa-8e66-87e843a7f7fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060875 #edb/ref 1067 "The Longer Leg" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186498606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186498624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186498636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1045 "30-60-90 Triangles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186498606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497797 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ec4d6c60-9493-5c8e-8def-a6cecde39a5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497870 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497870 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497870 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21e34be6-9d43-52e0-b22e-907ce34bc24d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497928 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497928 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497928 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39c1eea0-7c1a-5512-a40b-b00ac6438521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497983 #edb/ref 1080 "7\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417]